Upstream revision ported: v1.7.8 (56b87cda10fb394981849aa8de19b8491aea62b4, 2026-09-23).

The Zig translation re-implements the CommonMark/GFM parser subset of the following
upstream files (see tools/port-manifest.tsv for the machine-readable mapping):

  lex/lexer.go, lex/token.go
  ast/node.go (subset), ast/walk.go
  parse/parse.go, blocks.go, block_start.go, blockquote.go, paragraph.go,
        heading.go, thematic_break.go, list.go, html_block.go, code_block.go,
        code_span.go, link.go, inline_link.go, inlines.go, inline.go,
        delimiter.go, text.go, image.go, linkrefdef_index.go,
        linkrefdef_case_fold.go, auto_link.go, table.go, inline_html.go
  html/entity.go (generated tables), html/unesc_str.go, html/escape.go,
        html/escape_encode.go

No upstream source code is vendored into src/; it is translation with attribution.
The upstream Go tree is a git submodule at upstream/lute (pinned by the superproject
commit) and is used for differential testing and table generation only.

